{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"c6975ca76f9f667f1250ba403d0e6da2aafe14d0","body":"## Result\n\nA combinatorial proof of the projected discriminant/Hurwitz weight-polytope comparison requested by OWR-14299288-015, in the smooth, complete very ample, degree-at-least-two regime of the source's cited Sano theorem.\n\nThe argument combines a product-face centroid identity, finite-difference cancellation, equal-column regular refinements, and the established GKZ normal-fan compatibility. The support-function step proves the reverse inclusion without assuming that every projected discriminant vertex remains a vertex. The previously known geometric equality, GKZ foundations, Sano's analytic description, and Ogusu–Sano's surface inclusion are credited.\n\n## Scope\n\n- The complete proof is in `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/CANDIDATE.md`\n- Smoothness, complete lattice-point embeddings, and the source's degree hypothesis are retained\n- This is a combinatorial comparison within established GKZ theory, not a reconstruction of its foundations\n- Arbitrary singular or incomplete configurations are outside the claim\n- Historical novelty is unestablished\n\n## Independent validation\n\nA separate adversarial review passes the complete intended comparison and explicitly checks both the restored source hypotheses and requested proof type. The unchanged report and source-verification receipt are included under `review/`.\n\n- 1,227 author exact assertions, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- 8,093 independent exact lower-hull assertions, reproduced byte-for-byte\n- Frozen mathematical artifact SHA-256: `4931eccbb464b53af07b90e24b72060e681b9a7f1769c0030a9d7090e59b129c`\n\nThe finite checks are diagnostics alongside the general proof. This is separate AI review, not human peer review. Please keep this PR open as a draft for further examination.\n","files":[{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/QUEUE.md","additions":1,"deletions":1},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/CANDIDATE.md","additions":205,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/README.md","additions":19,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/RESEARCH_LOG.md","additions":23,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/SOURCES.md","additions":25,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/product_verification.json","additions":165,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/readiness.json","additions":26,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/review/REVIEW.md","additions":271,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/review/independent_checks.py","additions":293,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/review/independent_results.json","additions":80,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/review/review_summary.json","additions":35,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/review/source_verification.json","additions":48,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/source_manifest.json","additions":41,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/source_record.json","additions":72,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/status.json","additions":31,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/turns.jsonl","additions":1,"deletions":0},{"path":"unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30006309/verify_product_vectors.py","additions":133,"deletions":0}],"headRefName":"dot/math-30006309","headRefOid":"85c78d0cf3959d9d492a637cb90835ebc6a0e828","isDraft":true,"number":55,"state":"OPEN","title":"Give a reviewed combinatorial Hurwitz polytope comparison","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/55"}
